Z||000000||Coop88||08-17-2000||04:41 PM||||I have an 88formula with a v6. 140k miles. I pulled up in my drive and the engine started shaking and the tach was going nuts. It drove fine before I stopped. I figured the cat. convertor finally plugged up. So this morning I replaced the cat with a straight pipe. This is only temporary. The problem is, the engine is fine when it idles, but there is a huge loss in acceleration when I drive it, and the tach still goes nuts. No matter how far I push the gas, the acceleration is slow. The air filter is clean, I gave it a tune up about 1.5 months ago. Is it possible the cat damaged my engine? Or did something else break by coincidence? I've got no trouble codes. Does anyone have any ideas what's wrong with it? I'm moving tommorrow and I've gotta get it fixed ASAP. Just my luck.<p>[This message has been edited by Coop88 (edited 08-17-2000).]||||reg||9
