Z||000003||Coop88||08-17-2000||05:29 PM||||This is gonna sound dumb, but where/what is the tach filter? I disconnected the exhaust where it hooks up to the cat, and it does the same thing. The tach jumps instead of moving smoothly like it used to.||||reg||5
Z||000004||1FST2M6||08-17-2000||08:04 PM||||check and make sure the spark plug wires aren't arching to the intake.. my SE did that I KNEW i killed the motor cause it started with the nitrous runnin a friend in the car.. i was soo bummed...  i pulled into a parking lot (car still running) poped the deck lid and MUCH to my surprise.. it was a hole in a spark boot on the cap arcing to the intake... might also want to check the ignition control module.. they can last 100K miles or 10 minutes...||||reg||1
Z||000005||Phil||08-17-2000||09:10 PM||||Tach filter looks like a condenser it's mounted right by the dist.||||reg||1
